    {
      "name": "Bulk Load (Kafka)",
      "description": "Endpoints for bulk user load via asynchronous UUID pattern with Kafka processing.\n\nFlow:\n1. POST /api/users/bulk with ADMIN Basic Auth -> 202 Accepted + jobId\n2. GET /api/jobs/{jobId} to poll status -> ACCEPTED -> PROCESSING -> COMPLETED/PARTIAL/FAILED\n3. Check Kafka-UI at http://localhost:8085 for message flow\n\nSingle Load comparison:\n- POST /api/users -> 201 Created (synchronous, no Kafka)\n\nSee docs/architecture/bulk-vs-single-load.md for architecture details.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Single User Load",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "users"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Single Load lane: Synchronous/Reactive user creation via POST /api/users.\n\nReturns 201 Created with the user object. This endpoint is public (no Admin role required).\n\nRequest Body:\n- username (required)\n- password (required)\n- email (required, valid email format)"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Submit Bulk Job",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 202) {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('jobId', json.jobId);",
                  "    pm.test('Bulk job accepted - jobId saved', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(json.jobId).to.be.a('string');",
                  "        pm.expect(json.status).to.eql('ACCEPTED');",
                  "    });",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                {
                  "key": "username",
                  "value": "{{basicAuthUser}}",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "key": "password",
                  "value": "{{basicAuthPass}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{idempotencyKey}}",
                "description": "Optional. Prevents duplicate job submission when retrying."
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"options\": {\n    \"continueOnError\": true\n  },\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"clientRefId\": \"CSV-ROW-001\",\n      \"username\": \"bulkuser1\",\n      \"password\": \"BulkPass123!\",\n      \"email\": \"bulkuser1@example.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clientRefId\": \"CSV-ROW-002\",\n      \"username\": \"bulkuser2\",\n      \"password\": \"BulkPass456!\",\n      \"email\": \"bulkuser2@example.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"clientRefId\": \"CSV-ROW-003\",\n      \"username\": \"bulkuser3\",\n      \"password\": \"BulkPass789!\",\n      \"email\": \"bulkuser3@example.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users/bulk",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "users",
                "bulk"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Bulk Load lane: Asynchronous UUID pattern (ADMIN only).\n\nReturns 202 Accepted with a jobId UUID immediately. The job is dispatched to Kafka (profile=kafka) or processed in-memory (profile=!kafka).\n\nHeaders:\n- X-Idempotency-Key (optional): Prevents duplicate job submission on retry.\n\nRequest Body:\n- options.continueOnError (boolean): If true, processing continues even if some records fail.\n- records[]: Array of user objects (max 500).\n  - clientRefId (optional): Your reference ID for tracing.\n  - username (required)\n  - password (required, min 6 chars)\n  - email (required, valid format)\n\nRequires: Basic Auth with ADMIN credentials.\nThe test script auto-saves the returned jobId to the collection variable."
